  "texto": "Move one. The perfect start. They met at a friend's birthday party. By midnight he knew her coffee order, and the book she'd mentioned once. The next morning, a message. 'I haven't stopped thinking about you.' Flowers at her office. A playlist made just for her. A weekend trip, planned in secret. Week three. 'I've never felt like this about anyone.' Her friends were thrilled. Maya was thrilled. It felt like being chosen. Within a month, they were saying 'I love you.' Within two, he suggested she move in. There was one small moment she noticed. A flash of cold irritation when she was ten minutes late. She told herself it was nothing. Everyone has bad days. Here's what was actually happening. It has a name: love bombing. Overwhelming attention, fast, before you've had time to ask who this person really is. It isn't romance. It's a hook. And the faster it sets, the deeper it goes. Because when the warmth is suddenly taken away, you'll do almost anything to get it back. But Daniel wasn't finished. The next move didn't target Maya at all. It targeted everyone around her.",
  "voz": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
  "rate": "-4%",
  "capitulo": "C1",
  "nombre": "Move 1 - The perfect start (love bombing)"
